    "description": "Corrected oracle rolled forward by the 2026-10 farmland and regional-climate corrections (docs/integration/farmland-climate.md). Captured with the exact capture loops of tests/test_performance_equivalence.py and tests/test_governance_dormancy.py in Python off mode with the native ecology/politics runtimes disabled. Each workload index is the first turn that correction moves relative to the capture with all earlier corrections applied (consecutive captures). corrected_hunger_2026_10 and older fixtures remain frozen; workloads not named in 'corrections' are byte-identical to it.",
    "corrections": [
      {
        "id": "FC-FARM-RETURNS",
        "summary": "Diminishing returns to farm labour: the aggregate model's food yield (--agents off famine check) is scaled by food per head against constant returns, (L_ref + L_h) / (L + L_h) with farm labour L = 0.54 x population, L_ref = 0.33 x arable capacity (potential capacity raised by farming techniques and irrigation) and L_h = L_ref (output elasticity 0.5 at the reference). Agent modes: the native economy's farm labour is effective labour on the same curve and farmer income follows output per farmer.",
        "workloads": {
          "single": 5,
          "standard": 0,
          "wide": 9
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "FC-REGIONAL-CLIMATE",
        "summary": "Regional climate: the global phase keeps half of its crop and water effects (the long trend); the rest comes as regional harvest shocks, bad harvest years of clusters of up to three neighbouring regions (a two-state yearly chain, persistence 0.4, depth uniform 0.2-0.6) from namespaced stable_hash_int draws, which cut the region's crop climate factor and dry its land; the shares keep the cycle-mean crop factor and water budget of the global schedule.",
        "workloads": {
          "single": 0,
          "standard": 0,
          "wide": 26
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "FC-HUNGER-MAGNITUDES",
        "summary": "Hunger magnitudes raised part of the way to the mid range (deaths dearth 0.05 -> 0.10, famine 0.50 -> 1.00; births dearth 0.10 -> 0.15, famine 0.30 -> 0.45). In the aggregate model only the toll's share at a report's hunger moves (its ratio of the dearth and famine mortality terms).",
        "workloads": {}
      }
    ],
    "environment": {
      "python": "3.13.17",
      "platform": "Linux"
    }
  },
